{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 33, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III was a prominent figure in the Kingdom of Jerusalem during the 12th century.\n\n*Early Life and Succession*\nRaymond III was born around 1140. His father Raymond II was assassinated in 1152 and Raymond III succeeded him as Count of Tripoli. At the time Raymond III was still a minor and the regency was held by his mother Hodierna. In 1155 Raymond III came of age and took control of the county.\n\nRaymond III played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He was a member of the royal family and a cousin of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem. Raymond III supported King Baldwin III in his conflict with his mother Queen Melisende of Jerusalem. In 1157 Raymond III married Hodierna's niece Eschiva of Bures.\n\n*Conflict with Nur ad-Din*\nIn 1164 Raymond III was captured by the forces of Nur ad-Din during the Battle of Artah. He was held prisoner for several years and was eventually released in 1168. During his captivity the county was governed by his cousin Amalric of Nesle.\n\n*Later Life and Death*\nAfter his release from captivity Raymond III continued to play a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He supported King Amalric I of Jerusalem in his conflict with the Fatimid Caliphate. In 1174 Raymond III was appointed as regent for King Baldwin IV of Jerusalem. He held this position until his death in 1187. Raymond III died without an heir and the county of Tripoli passed to his godson Raymond IV Count of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004135505296289921}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.35154619812965393}, {"token": " of", "logprob":